  "schema": 1,
  "scope": "The whole original server compiled unchanged (as oracle/world-trace), booted as WorldTrace boots it (boot record byte-identical to the world-trace fixture's). Then the original constructor builds Players: for a fresh one and for each distinct character file the world-trace fixture holds, loaded with PlayerSaveParser.parse and runContentHooks. Recorded by reflection: every instance field of Node, Entity, Player, Properties, Skills, PlayerDetails, UserAccountInfo, UIDInfo, CommunicationInfo, SpellBookManager, FamiliarManager and Settings, as a value or, for other objects, as their class; registered quests, songs, the start location, save version and content hooks; generator positions and clock reads; PlayerSaver.populate's text and what each content hook wrote into it. Not covered: the field values of the other objects a Player holds, Player.init, login, ticks, other JDKs and operating systems.",
  "sourceHashAlgorithm": "sha256, CR removed",
